VERDICT: REJECTED
Primary conclusion: the diff introduces substantial Website Builder scaffolding, but it fails a core functional requirement—paid add-on activation via LemonSqueezy does not actually unlock/persist the feature.

Critical findings:
- **Blocking functional gap: webhook entitlement logic is missing for the add-on variant.** `POST /api/ls/website-addon-checkout` creates checkout for `LEMONSQUEEZY_WEBSITE_ADDON_VARIANT_ID`, but `POST /api/ls/webhook` never branches on that variant and never sets/clears `users.websiteAddonActive` or `websiteAddonSubscriptionId`. It only updates base `subscriptionTier/subscriptionExpiry` for monthly/yearly plan flow. Result: successful add-on purchase will not reliably unlock `/my-website` (which gates on `addonActive`), violating the “unlocks immediately and persists while active” requirement.
